    "text": "b) Let En be a free locally nilpotent n-Engel group on countably many\ngenerators, and let π(En ) be the set of prime divisors of the orders of elements of the\nperiodic part of En . It is known that 2, 3, 5 ∈ π(E4 ).\n   Is it true that π(En ) = π(En+1 ) for all sufficiently large n?     Yu. V. Sosnovskiı̆",
